import{_ as t,c as r,o as a,ag as n}from"./chunks/framework.Vyheyqg9.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Hub completion verification","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"review/verification.md","filePath":"review/verification.md"}'),i={name:"review/verification.md"};function o(s,e,d,c,l,p){return a(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="hub-completion-verification" tabindex="-1">Hub completion verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#hub-completion-verification" aria-label="Permalink to “Hub completion verification”">​</a></h1><p>Date: <strong>2026-10-27</strong>. <strong>All learner practice remains outstanding.</strong> This ledger separates fresh checks from preserved earlier evidence. No root dependency/script/template configuration or src/tests was changed.</p><h2 id="current-source-and-example-checks" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">1 </span>Current source and example checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#current-source-and-example-checks" aria-label="Permalink to “1 Current source and example checks”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Actual result</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engineering own-source compiler</td><td>TypeScript 5.9.3 with strict, noUncheckedIndexedAccess, exactOptionalPropertyTypes and explicit include scope passed</td><td>skipLibCheck retains the documented upstream declaration boundary; not every consumer fragment is in this compiler program</td></tr><tr><td>Focused state/utility runner</td><td>Relational snapshot atomicity/identity/isolation, B-before-A request ownership, cancellation, selector identity, HTTP schema/size/pre-abort/ignored-abort/stalled read, nonsettling cleanup, actual five-second deadline, local listener/history and debounce flush/cancel passed</td><td>Injected local adapters, no real network/browser/database or measured speed</td></tr><tr><td>Canonical source sweep</td><td>29 TS/TSX syntax transformations and 28 JS/CJS/MJS parse checks passed</td><td>Syntax is weaker than typechecking/runtime integration; generated build imports need the documented preceding build</td></tr><tr><td>Configuration TDD</td><td>Final 8 Node tests passed; isolated bad stub reproduced 3 pass/5 intended behavioral failures</td><td>Pure parser, controlled loader and temporary filesystem cleanup; no external service</td></tr><tr><td>Minimal quality standard</td><td>Actual npm run check passed lint→strict checkJs→1 behavior test→emit; unused/type/wrong-arithmetic variants each failed their intended command</td><td>Variants were applied only in a disposable copy and restored; no hosted gate or protected-branch setup</td></tr><tr><td>AI-engineering retry</td><td>Fresh pinned compiler install, build and all 7 emitted-artifact Node tests passed</td><td>Immediate bounded attempts, not transport/backoff/outer deadline or independent human review</td></tr><tr><td>Module assembly</td><td>Compound module fences split into real producer/consumer files; named/default consumers executed with expected output</td><td>Local ESM behavior only</td></tr><tr><td>Local Git and index generator</td><td>Git 2.54.0 disposable conflict→abort, recovery reference and staged-whitespace hook preserved index/worktree bytes; no remotes. Generator kept a curated index byte-identical and created a missing child index with ES6 label intact</td><td>No user history, remote push, hosted hooks or CI execution</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Node baseline: <strong>24.18.0</strong>. Checked dependency set: Toolkit 2.13.0, React 19.3.0, React Redux 9.3.0, Query 5.105.0, RxJS 7.8.2, Zod 4.6.7; quality fixture ESLint 10.13.0. Exact manifests/locks accompany isolated collections. These are reproducibility baselines, not blanket recommendations to upgrade a production project.</p><p>The source sweep exposed two compound modules treated as single files during extraction; the corrected split passes parsing and actual consumer execution. The authoritative HTTP race correction handles a pre-aborted owner without an unhandled rejected control promise and cancels a late abort-ignoring response body. Local cancellation cannot force remote work to stop or undo a write.</p><h2 id="documentation-and-compatibility" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">2 </span>Documentation and compatibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#documentation-and-compatibility" aria-label="Permalink to “2 Documentation and compatibility”">​</a></h2><p>The first whole-hub production build passed in 33.40 seconds; only the existing large-chunk warning remained. The initial full link check found three generated links to the same missing senior_growth.html route; the sidebar now points to the existing directory index. The subsequent production build passed in 32.45 seconds, followed by a zero-error full rendered local-link/fragment check. A final records-only rebuild is recorded in the live progress report. Across 109 changed existing rendered Markdown pages, no previous heading ID was lost.</p><p>Original routes/headings are retained where practical. The formerly extensionless Git lesson now has a real .md page, while its old local path is an explicit compatibility record with original digest. No previously built URL existed for that extensionless file. The index generator now preserves curated reading orders rather than overwriting them on rerun.</p><h2 id="inspection-and-inherited-evidence" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">3 </span>Inspection and inherited evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#inspection-and-inherited-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to “3 Inspection and inherited evidence”">​</a></h2><p>The current pass inspected actual explanatory ownership/failure/verification sections, compared overlapping Git/CI/state/quality explanations, and checked selected concrete source assemblies. It is not an exhaustive independent security review of every original code block, dependency or externally linked course. Exact files and depth/role are in the inventory; optional introductions do not claim an advanced second stack.</p><p>Completed Node/CS/applied-AI/frontend maps, source/workbench/practice organization and their dated verification limits remain authoritative for those files. Previous browser/database/container/provider-model checks were <strong>not all rerun</strong>. Original historical reports and summary remain unchanged; the live summary is CURRENT_LEARNING_SUMMARY.md. Earlier progress bodies remain verbatim beneath the current completion record.</p><p>Official behavior references rechecked 2026-10-27: <a href="https://redux.js.org/usage/deriving-data-selectors" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Redux selectors</a>, <a href="https://redux-toolkit.js.org/api/createAsyncThunk" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">async-thunk cancellation</a>, <a href="https://git-scm.com/docs/git-worktree" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Git worktrees</a>, <a href="https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/jobs/job_artifacts/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitLab artifact handoffs</a>, <a href="https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/commands/npm-ci" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">npm ci</a>, <a href="https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jest snapshot review</a>, <a href="https://web.dev/articles/vitals" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Core Web Vitals</a>, <a href="https://top10.owasp.org/2025/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OWASP Top 10:2025</a>. Existing tested version/date qualifiers are preserved instead of silently upgrading every alternative.</p><h2 id="specific-unperformed-verification-and-learner-work" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">4 </span>Specific unperformed verification and learner work <a class="header-anchor" href="#specific-unperformed-verification-and-learner-work" aria-label="Permalink to “4 Specific unperformed verification and learner work”">​</a></h2><p>No new screen-reader, text/page zoom, physical-device, cross-engine, translation/fluent-review, contrast certification, browser memory/performance trace or approved pixel baseline was performed in this completion pass. New documentation desktop/mobile checks do not establish those results. Keep every prior open matrix item open until actually observed.</p><p>No hosted CI, cloud/IAM effectiveness, paid service, workflow publication, live identity/model provider, production traffic/cost/SLO, multi-region system, load benchmark or deployed backup restore was activated or inferred. Pure schema/compatibility models are not database/deployment tests. Linked original PostgreSQL/container checks retain only their stated local evidence; each learner integration still needs its own results.</p><p>External authenticated/paid courses and presentation links are bibliographic pointers; unseen content, availability and learner completion are not certified. Introductory AWS/Kubernetes/graph database/microfrontend/alternate renderer/RxJS topics remain bounded optional depth, with the E07 comparison option rather than a mandatory production implementation for each.</p><h2 id="current-documentation-browser-observations" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">5 </span>Current documentation browser observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#current-documentation-browser-observations" aria-label="Permalink to “5 Current documentation browser observations”">​</a></h2><p>Installed Chrome 156.0.8078.48 on macOS, controlled headlessly with Playwright 1.58.2: eight representative desktop routes (1360×960) and six mobile-width routes (390×844) loaded without page exceptions; mobile routes had no document-width overflow. Both new Mermaid processes rendered SVG without renderer errors. Visual inspection confirmed a clear security-boundary diagram and readable mobile workbench hierarchy; wide tables use their own scroll area. Space on the focused Learning paths button exposed the Frontend link. Escape was sent, but menu closure was not asserted. The downloadable inventory returned all 1,077 records with no pending essential-review rows. These observations apply to documentation navigation/layout, not native execution of every embedded application.</p>',19)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
